Review note

Reason:
The context meter was still selecting the Ollama system-prompt tier from the model name, while chat execution uses Ollama parameter_size metadata. Custom or opaque model names could therefore display a context cost for a prompt different from the one actually injected.

Design:
- context_usage_memory::usage now returns one ResolvedContextUsage containing both memory usage and the prompt tier from the same context_resolve call;
- API providers retain the existing name/catalog fallback because their ContextWindows intentionally has no Ollama prompt tier;
- estimate_context_hidden_usage consumes that resolved tier before building and measuring the prompt, without adding another /api/show request;
- the Modelfile prompt panel identity includes promptTier so a modelfile-updated event that crosses the 25B boundary remounts cleanly;
- the unreachable loadErrorKey branch inside ModelfileView parameters was removed; load failures remain handled by the outer alert.

TDD / mutation evidence:
- before implementation, the Rust metadata-precedence test did not compile because the authority helper did not exist;
- before the React key fix, the remount test stayed on compact after rerendering detailed;
- mutation back to tier_for_model in context_usage.rs makes hidden_usage_resolves_context_before_selecting_the_prompt fail;
- mutation back to key={modelName} makes modelfile-view-prompt-tier.test.tsx fail.

